WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.912 --> 00:00:16.193
could we move that heavy boat?

2
00:00:17.013 --> 00:00:19.314
I stood on the deck, looking at the wreckage around us.

3
00:00:19.334 --> 00:00:21.415
"We need a lever and rollers!"

4
00:00:21.495 --> 00:00:21.915
I cried.

5
00:00:21.935 --> 00:00:24.776
"Fetch me a sturdy wooden plank for a lever.

6
00:00:25.476 --> 00:00:27.817
We can make rollers from what's left of a mast."

7
00:00:31.579 --> 00:00:34.440
Fritz quickly brought a plank, and I cut up a mast.

8
00:00:35.724 --> 00:00:39.907
Then I raised the bow of our boat with the plank while my sons placed a roller under

9
00:00:39.947 --> 00:00:44.210
it. We repeated the process, placing two more rollers under the boat.

10
00:00:47.332 --> 00:00:51.175
When we once again began to push, we were able to launch our boat into the water.

11
00:00:55.298 --> 00:00:58.980
my beloved family," I announced, "it's time to make our escape.

12
00:00:59.381 --> 00:01:01.122
Leave plenty of food near the animals.

13
00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:04.024
Then collect everything that may be of use to us."

14
00:01:04.896 --> 00:01:06.477
The boys joyfully obeyed me.

15
00:01:07.658 --> 00:01:13.461
From the large quantity of things they gathered, I chose canvas for a tent, a chest of carpenter's

16
00:01:13.521 --> 00:01:19.645
tools, fishing rods, an iron pot, cases of biscuits and dried soup, and some other items.

17
00:01:20.805 --> 00:01:24.227
We now began to take our seats, each one of us in our own tub.

18
00:01:24.888 --> 00:01:28.650
Just then we heard the roosters crowing as if scolding us for abandoning them.

19
00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:31.632
"Let's take them with us," urged my wife.

20
00:01:34.856 --> 00:01:39.037
So we placed ten hens and a couple of roosters in one tub with some wire netting over

21
00:01:39.077 --> 00:01:39.457
the top.

22
00:01:43.579 --> 00:01:48.040
The ducks and geese took to the water at once while the pigeons swiftly flew toward shore.

23
00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:56.403
is my contribution," said my wife, throwing a mysterious bag to Franz.

24
00:01:57.423 --> 00:02:00.624
All being ready, we cast off and moved away from the wreck.

25
00:02:04.756 --> 00:02:07.357
My good, brave wife sat in the first compartment.

26
00:02:07.997 --> 00:02:12.258
Then came Franz, our youngest son, followed by Fritz, our oldest son.

27
00:02:12.938 --> 00:02:15.279
The center tubs contained our valuable cargo.

28
00:02:16.119 --> 00:02:22.241
Then came our third son, bold Jack, followed by Ernest, our intelligent but rather lazy second son.

29
00:02:23.101 --> 00:02:26.842
I stood in the stern, trying to guide the boat to a safe landing place.

30
00:02:28.002 --> 00:02:31.443
We had left the two large dogs, Turk and Juno on the wreck.

31
00:02:32.184 --> 00:02:35.769
But when they saw us deserting them, they sprang into the sea after us.

32
00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:40.171
As we neared the shore, it appeared rocky and barren.

33
00:02:43.013 --> 00:02:48.096
The geese and ducks, however, found an opening between the rocks where a stream flowed into the sea.

34
00:02:49.216 --> 00:02:53.459
I steered after them, and we soon found ourselves in a small, calm bay.

35
00:02:58.721 --> 00:03:03.184
As soon as we could gather our children around us on dry land, we knelt in prayer.

36
00:03:04.116 --> 00:03:06.638
Then together we unloaded the boat and set up a tent.

37
00:03:07.779 --> 00:03:10.561
The younger boys quickly gathered moss and grass for beds.

38
00:03:11.801 --> 00:03:14.984
I made a fireplace with some large flat stones near the brook.

39
00:03:16.204 --> 00:03:19.366
Then my wife began making soup with the help of little Franz.

40
00:03:19.386 --> 00:03:22.108
"Mama, don't you want some beef?"

41
00:03:22.529 --> 00:03:24.850
he asked as she added water to the dried soup.

42
00:03:25.711 --> 00:03:26.952
"Where can I get it, dear?"

43
00:03:27.292 --> 00:03:28.052
she reminded him.

44
00:03:28.072 --> 00:03:30.714
"We're a long way from a butcher's shop."

45
00:03:31.795 --> 00:03:33.156
"Oh," he said quietly.

46
00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:37.342
Meanwhile Fritz climbed over the rocks to see what lay beyond the stream.

47
00:03:38.102 --> 00:03:42.224
That kind of brisk exercise didn't suit Ernest, so he wandered down to the beach.

48
00:03:43.684 --> 00:03:46.405
Jack scrambled among the rocks searching for shellfish.

49
00:03:47.626 --> 00:03:50.607
I was eager to grab two casks that had been floating near our boat.

50
00:03:51.227 --> 00:03:53.928
While struggling to do that, I heard Jack cry out.

51
00:03:55.129 --> 00:03:56.930
"Help!" he screamed.

52
00:03:57.710 --> 00:04:02.092
Fearing he was in great danger, I ran and found him standing in a deep pool.

53
00:04:03.056 --> 00:04:05.878
A huge lobster had caught his leg in its powerful claw!

54
00:04:06.899 --> 00:04:08.400
Poor Jack was very frightened.

55
00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:10.701
"It won't let me go!"

56
00:04:11.062 --> 00:04:11.562
he cried.

57
00:04:12.343 --> 00:04:15.285
I grabbed the lobster firmly by the back, and it released its grip.

58
00:04:15.965 --> 00:04:18.327
Jack carried the lobster triumphantly to the tent.

59
00:04:19.848 --> 00:04:23.730
He urged his mother to add it to the soup, but she decided to save it for another

60
00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:26.813
meal. "Congratulations, Jack," I said.

61
00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:29.014
"You're the first to discover something useful."

62
00:04:29.795 --> 00:04:31.456
"I found something good to eat too.

63
00:04:31.928 --> 00:04:33.349
Oysters!" said Ernest.

64
00:04:37.651 --> 00:04:39.192
I didn't want to get my feet wet.

65
00:04:39.893 --> 00:04:42.494
And I found sea salt in the crevices of the rocks."

66
00:04:44.495 --> 00:04:47.457
"Never let me hear you object to getting your feet wet," I said.

67
00:04:48.277 --> 00:04:50.539
"See how quickly the sun has dried Jack and me."

68
00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:54.441
My wife stirred the soup with a stick.

69
00:04:54.461 --> 00:04:59.724
"Our soup is ready, but how will we eat it without bowls or spoons?"

70
00:05:00.732 --> 00:05:01.553
"Oyster shells!"

71
00:05:01.853 --> 00:05:02.674
Ernest exclaimed.

72
00:05:03.715 --> 00:05:05.437
The boys ran off to get some oysters.

73
00:05:10.381 --> 00:05:15.065
By the time they came back, Fritz had also returned with reports of the beautiful country that lay

74
00:05:15.125 --> 00:05:15.886
beyond the stream.

75
00:05:19.549 --> 00:05:22.432
We ate the oysters and scooped up our soup with the shells.

76
00:05:25.755 --> 00:05:30.643
As the sun set, my wife pulled some oats from her mysterious bag and fed the poultry.

77
00:05:32.604 --> 00:05:35.026
Our first day ashore drew peacefully to a close.
